      "summary": ": Wednesday, 2 September: Cardrona is open with excellent freshly groomed cord on piste, while off-piste terrain is variable, ranging from fresh pockets to very firm areas. It is around 3°C with strong winds, gusting to 92 km/h, and the wind is expected to increase through the day. There has been no fresh snow in the last 24 hours, with 63 cm recorded over the past seven days. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, Valley View and T-Bar are open. Whitestar Express is on hold, while McDougall’s Chondola, Captains Express, Soho Express and Willow’s Quad are closed. McDougall’s and Captains have been closed for the day due to increased wind, while Soho and Willows have also closed for the day. Guests should take care when heading off piste because of the mix of fresh snow and firm areas. Seven of nine terrain parks are open, including Baby Bucks, Little Bucks, Antlers Alley, Stag Lane, Big Bucks, Peoples Pipe and Gravity Cross; Olympic Pipe and Big Air are closed. The Wells Pipe Platter is closed after its morning operating window for the Olympic Halfpipe. Road access is chain-free, but chains should be carried and an active road hazard remains. Shuttle buses are running from the bottom of Valley View to return guests to base as wind affects upper-mountain lift access.",
